      "worked_solution": "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n5(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={20}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {20}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n5(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘})=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}.\n$$",
